# Healing Shaman

**Alignments.** Any, but tends to be good; the spirits avoid selfish people.

Among the most powerful healing psionics on Rifts Earth, rivalled only by the
Gypsy Gifted of Germany, combining great psychic healing with a little healing
magic to keep the Native American peoples, and every creature the Circle of Life
depends on, alive and well. Most keep to a Preserve or tribal camp where the
sick and wounded come to them; others wander the wilds, sometimes guided by the
spirits to the lost and injured who have been given up for dead.

## Lore

Their greatest works happen in the Sweat Lodges - a handful of legendary
fetishes kept by greater spirits in remote and secret places, perhaps moved by
the spirits after every use. There a gathering of Shamans can regrow limbs and
even raise the dead, and the lodges'' locations are kept secret on pain of death.

## Equipment the catalog cannot hold yet

Ceremonial garments and headdress, a hat or hooded cloak, moccasins, a hand
axe, a scalpel, sewing needles, thread, three rolls of gauze, a bag of healing
herbs, flint, 50 feet of rope, a ball of string, a week of dried food, a mixing
bowl, a grinding stone, a small lidded pot, a mallet, 2D4 wooden stakes and a
silver cross. Two S.D.C. weapons of choice, usually a large knife, tomahawk or
war club.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'healing-shaman');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'healing-shaman';

